---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_ENTITY, LOCATION } from '../config';
const updated = '12 October 2026';
const TBC = '[TO BE COMPLETED]';
---
<Base title="Privacy notice — mendelX" description="How mendelX handles the personal data you share through the pilot programme form.">
  <article class="privacy wrap">
    <header>
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="h2">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Who we are</h2>
      <p>mendelX is an early-stage agricultural technology company founded by Pavlos Mazomenos and Dr. Georgios Athanasiou. We are responsible (the “data controller”) for the personal data described in this notice.</p>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li><span>Legal entity</span>{LEGAL_ENTITY || TBC}</li>
        <li><span>Address</span>{LOCATION || TBC}</li>
        <li><span>Contact</span>{CONTACT_EMAIL ? <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> : TBC}</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you apply to our pilot programme, we collect the details you enter in the form: your name, email address, phone number (optional), region or location, farm size, main crops, tractor brand and model (optional), and any message you choose to add. We also record that you gave consent.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>We use these details only to assess pilot applications and to contact you about the mendelX pilot programme. We do not sell your data or use it for advertising.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Legal basis</h2>
      <p>We process your data on the basis of your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you give by ticking the consent box on the form. You can withdraw your consent at any time; this does not affect processing carried out before you withdrew it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Who processes it</h2>
      <p>Form submissions are received through Formspree, a form-handling service that acts as our data processor and delivers submissions to us. Formspree may process data outside the European Economic Area under appropriate safeguards such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses. Our website is hosted on GitHub Pages, which, like any web host, processes technical data such as IP addresses to deliver the site.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep your details until the pilot programme ends, or until you ask us to delete them, whichever comes first.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to access the data we hold about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to restrict or object to its processing, to receive it in a portable format, and to withdraw your consent at any time. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at the address above.</p>
      <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Hellenic Data Protection Authority (<a href="https://www.dpa.gr" rel="noopener">www.dpa.gr</a>).</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Analytics</h2>
      <p>We may use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits to this site. It does not use cookies, does not track you across websites and does not build personal profiles, which is why this site shows no cookie banner.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy { max-width: 820px; padding-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 72px); padding-bottom: 120px; display: grid; gap: 48px; }
  header { display: grid; gap: 20px; }
  .updated { color: var(--text-dim); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 12.5px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  section { display: grid; gap: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 28px; }
  section p { color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 64ch; }
  section a { color: var(--text); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .facts { list-style: none; margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 8px; color: var(--text); }
  .facts span { display: inline-block; width: 140px; color: var(--text-dim); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 12.5px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
</style>
